    <name>Parallel Consumer - Proxy Client Scala</name>
    <artifactId>parallel-consumer-proxy-client-scala</artifactId>

    <!--
        SKELETON, deliberately - and the second client with NO foreign-toolchain wrapper, for the
        same reason as Kotlin: Scala is a JVM language and builds with Maven directly
        (scala-maven-plugin, from Central like any other plugin), so it needs nothing installed
        that the JVM reactor does not already have. sbt is the ecosystem's usual build tool and is
        deliberately NOT used here - it would be a second build system in a Maven reactor, and the
        wave that writes this client should reach for it only if the Maven plugin genuinely cannot
        express what Scala needs.

        Seeded after the first fan-out wave rather than with the original nine, so unlike its
        siblings this module has no CI row in .github/workflows/clients.yml yet - the Scala wave
        adds one, mirroring the shape of the other rows. Its wave owns everything in this
        directory, including the build wiring and the static-analysis setup that every other
        client module carries.
    -->

</project>
